# Minimal profile: base interpreters + safe-by-default overrides.
#
# Line 1 (above) is the space-separated list of variables 'environment init'
# copies from template/environment/ into .env/default/. Everything below is
# documentation.
#
# Security model:
# - TERMINAL_INTERPRETER defaults to 'cat' (display-only, safe by default).
# - State-changing commands (setenv/getenv/unsetenv/printenv/error/fail/
#   environment cache) are pinned to 'sh' so they still take effect.
# - The bookkeeping terminals of the templates (mint, unlink, leaf write,
#   leaf erase, line append, line remove, line mask) are pinned to sh so
#   that add, drop and mask act directly; the display terminals (list, show
#   head, line table, dump record) to cat so their text survives an
#   executing terminal default.
# - Users override anything by writing files into .env/local/ (setenv).
